# Tracker files — see docs/technical/11-work-tracking.md (D-11.6, §5).

# Append-only audit of field changes: keep both sides' new lines, never conflict.
.beads/interactions.jsonl merge=union
# Projection of the bd graph: never text-merged — on conflict regenerate with `bd export`.
.beads/issues.jsonl merge=binary

# Visual-regression baselines — see docs/technical/08-testing-quality.md (D-08.10, INV-08.8).

# One reviewed PNG per shot. `merge=binary` is stated rather than left to git's
# content sniffing, because it is the whole reason these may be tracked where
# reports/content-coverage.md may not (D-08.20). That file was a derived
# aggregate in one text file, so two branches each adding one key both wrote the
# same new total and git merged them to a number that was wrong. A screenshot is
# neither aggregate nor shared: disjoint shots merge cleanly, the same shot
# conflicts loudly, and the conflict is resolved by regenerating in the
# Playwright container and looking at the picture.
tests/e2e/__screenshots__/**/*.png merge=binary -diff
